WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.140
A student with a teacher.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.410
A householder with a family.

3
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.860
A retiree turning to prayer.

4
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.500
A renouncer with only a
cloth and a water pot.

5
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.490
Hindu tradition sets
out these four stages,

6
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.700
often pictured as about 25 years each.

7
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.120
Each stage has its own duties.

8
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.470
And traditionally, so
did each class of birth.

9
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.040
Must every Hindu follow these stages?

10
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.060
And can love of God break the rules?

11
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.610
In this mission, you'll see why one stage,

12
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.290
the householder, is said
to hold up all the others.

13
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.180
Then you'll trace
poet-saints across India,

14
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.280
and ask whether the
stages still matter today.

15
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.080
Your mission: find out how
Hindus live out the stages,

16
00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.370
and what devotion does to the rules.
